## Description

This is the second version of my personal portfolio. It starts from my
Assignment 1 site (pastel "folder-card" design, built with plain HTML, CSS and
JavaScript) and makes it more interactive: visitors are greeted by name, can
filter and search my projects, and the page animates as they scroll.

There are no frameworks, libraries, build tools or backend. Everything runs in
the browser from static files.

## What's New Since Assignment 1

| Requirement | Feature |
|---|---|
| **Dynamic content** | **Project filter + live search.** Category buttons (All / UI/UX / Web) and a search box that filters the project cards as you type. They work together. |
| **Dynamic content** | **Personalised greeting.** The hero greets the visitor with "Good morning / afternoon / evening" based on their local time, plus their name once they enter it. |
| **Data handling** | **`localStorage`.** The visitor's name is validated, saved and restored on the next visit ("Not you?" forgets it). The dark/light theme is saved too. |
| **Animation** | **Scroll animations.** Sections fade and slide in as they scroll into view, with staggered timing for skill pills and project cards. |
| **Animation** | **Hover effects** on project cards (lift, image zoom, tab growth, tag colour, arrow nudge), skill pills, filter buttons and buttons. |
| **Error handling and feedback** | Friendly validation messages for the name field, an **empty state** ("No projects found") with a *Clear filters* button, a live result count ("Showing 1 of 2 projects"), and animated confirmation/error messages. |

Other improvements: the site respects `prefers-reduced-motion`, works without
JavaScript (content stays visible, interactive controls are hidden), has visible
keyboard focus styles, and announces filter results to screen readers.

